%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 118899cb856d7e04bac83f4463fd3b31, type: 3}
  m_Name: Scene07Dialogue
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::AdaptiveOhmsLaw.DialogueSequence
  lines:
  - id: intro_test
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: Let's put your prediction to the test.
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 2a132aec787872945ac1a4ae02189eb8, type: 3}
    duration: 2.8989797
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
    overrideCinematicSubject: 0
    cinematicSubject: 0
  - id: recall_increase
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: You predicted that the current would increase. Let's collect some evidence.
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 47f1593bff6c76d40ba50b37ef32291f, type: 3}
    duration: 5.398481
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
    overrideCinematicSubject: 0
    cinematicSubject: 0
  - id: recall_decrease
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: You predicted that the current would decrease. Let's investigate what the
      meter tells us.
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: a3bb6e1c7321e6a4da731cd05b2d295b, type: 3}
    duration: 6.1484127
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
    overrideCinematicSubject: 0
    cinematicSubject: 0
  - id: recall_same
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: You predicted that the current would stay the same. Let's compare a few
      measurements.
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 61fbdf8c24b1b3445841c2c08b0721ce, type: 3}
    duration: 5.878481
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
    overrideCinematicSubject: 0
    cinematicSubject: 0
  - id: intro_neutral
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: Let's investigate how potential difference affects current in this circuit.
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: df68c49b40924cb4dafda05c6e27938c, type: 3}
    duration: 4.618526
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
    overrideCinematicSubject: 0
    cinematicSubject: 0
  - id: intro_same_resistor
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: We will keep the same wire at constant temperature and change only the
      potential difference. Collect readings at one, two, three, four and five volts.
    audio: {fileID: 0}
    duration: 10
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
    overrideCinematicSubject: 0
    cinematicSubject: 0
  - id: guide_supported
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: Close the circuit switch first to complete the path, then turn the knob
      to 1 V and record your reading.
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 1f8528abd227c9748a412046acacf8de, type: 3}
    duration: 6.70805
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
    overrideCinematicSubject: 0
    cinematicSubject: 0
  - id: guide_guided
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: Close the switch, then turn the knob to record readings at each whole volt
      from one to five volts.
    audio: {fileID: 0}
    duration: 7.6
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
    overrideCinematicSubject: 0
    cinematicSubject: 0
  - id: reading_recorded
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: Reading recorded in the table. Turn the knob to the next voltage.
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 04235fe0ce4faf2448de4fc74923653f, type: 3}
    duration: 5.0735373
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
    overrideCinematicSubject: 0
    cinematicSubject: 0
  - id: readings_complete
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: All five readings recorded. Notice the pattern in your observation table.
    audio: {fileID: 0}
    duration: 4.4
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
    overrideCinematicSubject: 0
    cinematicSubject: 0
  - id: evidence_prompt
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: With the resistance kept the same, what happened to the current as the
      voltage increased?
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: e8327711ce8b22e4d8fc9e23bfd17d44, type: 3}
    duration: 5.578345
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
    overrideCinematicSubject: 0
    cinematicSubject: 0
  - id: evidence_accepted
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: Our readings show that increasing the voltage increased the current through
      this resistor.
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 8d68121ff049c5945b80e379b27ce3cb, type: 3}
    duration: 5.053447
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
    overrideCinematicSubject: 0
    cinematicSubject: 0
  - id: prediction_matched
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: Your prediction matches the evidence we collected!
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: fcc8b7a94e0f1f449b64af51d6755150, type: 3}
    duration: 3.4687755
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
    overrideCinematicSubject: 0
    cinematicSubject: 0
  - id: prediction_revised
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: The measurements gave us new evidence. Revising a prediction is part of
      doing science.
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: a45cfb116bcac454c95aac9c1e79d1d9, type: 3}
    duration: 6.3681407
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
    overrideCinematicSubject: 0
    cinematicSubject: 0
  - id: evidence_clue
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: Take another look at the observation table. Compare the current at 1.0
      V with 3.0 V.
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 038a1e1ced9dfba4e94a2e06dfb9d83f, type: 3}
    duration: 7.608095
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
    overrideCinematicSubject: 0
    cinematicSubject: 0
  - id: evidence_supported_clue
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: At one volt, current is 0.20 amperes. At three volts, current is 0.60 amperes.
      The current increased.
    audio: {fileID: 0}
    duration: 6.8
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
    overrideCinematicSubject: 0
    cinematicSubject: 0
  - id: evidence_retry
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: Compare the five readings and choose the answer that fits our data.
    audio: {fileID: 0}
    duration: 4.8
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
    overrideCinematicSubject: 0
    cinematicSubject: 0
  - id: evidence_guided_complete
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: 'Let''s look at the evidence together: the table confirms that current
      increased as voltage increased.'
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 3c0444c85659ba54b80e28bdf44c2680, type: 3}
    duration: 6.4582086
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
    overrideCinematicSubject: 0
    cinematicSubject: 0
  - id: scene_complete
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: Great scientific investigation! You have verified how current depends on
      potential difference.
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: bc217aaa844133b46a313eb9504c72ad, type: 3}
    duration: 6.9181633
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
    overrideCinematicSubject: 0
    cinematicSubject: 0
  - id: final_handoff
    speaker: WATTSON
    text: Let's turn these measurements into a graph and look for a pattern.
    audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 27ba0a6eec98863418a9a1f1d8e283b7, type: 3}
    duration: 4.2235603
    emotion: Curious
    nextEvent: 
    overrideCinematicSubject: 0
    cinematicSubject: 0
